        ["a","b","*","c"]  -> equivalent list form
    - label_path: optional path relative to each wildcard match used to extract labels for the x-axis.
      If your key_path includes a '*' it will produce one numeric value per matched element; label_path
      will be applied relative to the matched element to produce a label for that element.
    - kind: one of 'line', 'bar', 'hist', 'scatter'
    - Returns: (values, labels) where labels may be None if not provided or unavailable.

    Lightweight plotting: uses matplotlib if available; otherwise prints a small ASCII histogram.

    Example usage:
      data = {"items":[{"name":"a","v":1},{"name":"b","v":3},{"name":"c","v":2}]}
      visualize_json_numbers(data, "items.*.v", label_path="name", kind="bar", title="Example")
    """
    # local imports so function is copy-paste friendly
    from collections.abc import Mapping, Sequence
    import math

    # helper to parse path
    if isinstance(key_path, str):
